  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Develop Capabilities / Drop PE Stub", "technique": "T1587.001", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-14 08:11:03 CEST, Wazuh FIM detected the creation of C:\\ProgramData\\MicrosoftUpdate\\maintenance_check.exe on agent wafaawindows (10.108.57.177). The path C:\\ProgramData\\MicrosoftUpdate\\ is NOT a legitimate Microsoft update directory — it is an attacker-created directory designed to masquerade as a Microsoft infrastructure folder. FIM fired syscheck.event=added on a PE (.exe) file under a monitored ProgramData subtree.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh FIM rule (rule.id 554, syscheck.event=added) fired on syscheck.path=C:\\ProgramData\\MicrosoftUpdate\\maintenance_check.exe. ProgramData is in the Wazuh FIM monitored-paths list. The combination of a newly appeared PE in a fake-Microsoft-named subdirectory is a high-confidence drop indicator.", "first_seen": "2026-05-14T08:11:03+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Defense Evasion / Signature Validation", "technique": "T1587.001", "what_happened": "At 08:13:27 CEST (~2 min after the drop), Sysmon Event 7 (ImageLoad) fired on wafaawindows for maintenance_check.exe with data.win.eventdata.signed=false and data.win.eventdata.signatureStatus=NotSigned. Wazuh custom rule 92500 fired: 'Unsigned PE executed from anomalous path'. The binary bears no Authenticode signature — it is an attacker-compiled loader with no code-signing certificate, distinguishing it from any legitimate Microsoft component.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon EID 7 ImageLoad: data.win.eventdata.image=C:\\ProgramData\\MicrosoftUpdate\\maintenance_check.exe + data.win.eventdata.signed=false + data.win.eventdata.signatureStatus=NotSigned → rule 92500 fires. The unsigned+anomalous-path combination is the canonical custom-malware binary fingerprint under MITRE T1587.001.", "first_seen": "2026-05-14T08:13:27+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Execution / Unsigned Binary Launch", "technique": "T1204", "what_happened": "At 08:14:09 CEST, Sysmon Event 1 (ProcessCreate) fired: data.win.eventdata.image=C:\\ProgramData\\MicrosoftUpdate\\maintenance_check.exe, data.win.eventdata.parentImage=C:\\Windows\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe, data.win.eventdata.commandLine=\"C:\\ProgramData\\MicrosoftUpdate\\maintenance_check.exe\". Wazuh custom rule 92501 fired: 'AppData/ProgramData binary execute + low prevalence'. The binary was launched by PowerShell — consistent with a script-based dropper (Start-Process in a PS1 loader). The parent PowerShell process is the delivery vehicle; maintenance_check.exe is the payload.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon EID 1 ProcessCreate: data.win.eventdata.image=*maintenance_check.exe + data.win.eventdata.parentImage=*powershell.exe → rule 92501. PowerShell parent + unsigned ProgramData child is the hallmark of a script-based dropper delivery chain. MITRE T1204 (User Execution) covers the operator-triggered execution via a prepared PS1 script.", "first_seen": "2026-05-14T08:14:09+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Defense Evasion / Execution Telemetry Injection", "technique": "T1587.001", "what_happened": "At 08:22:14 CEST, Wazuh syslog rule fired on a Windows Event Log entry written by maintenance_check.exe into the Application event log: Source='MicrosoftUpdateAgent', EventID=1001, Message='Update check completed successfully'. This is a fake event-log entry generated by the attacker binary to blend its execution into legitimate Windows Update telemetry. The binary deliberately masquerades as a Microsoft Update component at both the filesystem-path level (ProgramData\\MicrosoftUpdate\\) and the event-log level (MicrosoftUpdateAgent source).", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule firing on Windows Application Event Log: EventID=1001, Source=MicrosoftUpdateAgent written by maintenance_check.exe process. Masquerading via fake event-source registration is MITRE T1036.004 (Masquerading: Match Legitimate Name or Location). The combination of unsigned binary + fake MS Update path + fake event-log telemetry confirms a purpose-built attacker tool (not accidental or misconfigured software).", "first_seen": "2026-05-14T08:22:14+0200"}
